In class activity - Think Like an AI Designer

For the problem identified in previous assignment , Please complete the following
What are the features?
A-History of sales, current inventory, lead times, seasonal demand, industry trends
Identify the information that the model could use as inputs.
A-Sales, inventory, lead times, seasonal demand, industry trends
What is the label?
A- The label is the future demand for a pruduct made by the company, the model should be able to predict the future demand of customers using previous data and seasonality.
What are the inputs?
A-sales, inventory, lead times, seasonal demand, industry trends
What outcome should the model learn to predict?
A- the model should learn to predict future demand
What would training data contain?
A- training data would include previous inventory data and seasonal demand, the trends of the industry and lead times so the model can use all important variables when determining inventory levels
Why should testing data be kept separate?
A- testing data and real world real time data should be kept seperate because the real time updated data may not have the same outcomes as if both were used and the real time data is showing whats currently happening, the training data is just that, for training
What could be a false positive?
A- calling for more inventory than needed
What could be a false negative?
A-calling for less inventory than needed
Would precision or recall be more important?
A- Precision
Explain your reasoning.
A- Recalling old information would be important for seasonality, but the precision of the model is where the money is saved, if it calls for too much product it costs money to store, if it calls for too little there is stockouts and lost earnings due to a loss in sales.

What types of poor-quality data could affect this model?
A-incorrect data could offset outputs, leading to over or under stocking, increasing costs incurred by the company.
What could cause this model to overfit?
A- if it focuses too much on historical data and not newwer data,
What would make you trust—or not trust—the model's predictions?
A-If the model is fixating on past data and not including newer relevant data i would be worried about the accuracy, if it is only focusing on new data and not including seasonality i would also be worried, it needs to incorporate both into its predictions.